Total Japanese-MMO garbage, and if you've played many of these before, you'll know exactly what I mean. The only reason to play this game is for the Digimon branding, that is its single 'pro'. The 'cons' are inumerable:
The translation is terrible - utterly broken English on the verge of being unintelligible;
The gameplay is pure grinding - literally no other missions than "go to X and kill Y, and hope they drop Z";
The gameplay is boring - double-click on the enemy and watch your digimon hit it - when it's done, click on the dropped items to pick up, and repeat;
Everything is locked behind chance - you'll get mission items from maybe 60% of your enemies, you can't get a new Digimon without passing a 50-50 flip of the coin three times (which consumes items each time, and you lose the digiegg if you fail, which is a rare item in itself), and if you want new digieggs, or anything for that matter, be prepared to grind for tens of minutes for one item;
The world is free-for-all - whoever hits the enemy first gets the rewards, so people will camp areas and no one else will get anything. Respawn rates are so slow that a single player can keep an area entirely unpopulated, making missions impossible until they leave. Similarly, if someone knows where a boss will spawn, they let everyone else do the pre-event killing and reap the rewards themselves.
Everything is locked behind the cash-shop - don't want your inventory to be full or garbage after 20 minutes of grinding? want to get anything more than the absolute base stats? want to look like anything but the filthy F2P player that you are? Better get your Steam Wallet ready. Fashion items are timed - you don't buy anything, merely rent it. Digivolutions are locked behind specific items, which you need to buy. Want more than a 50% chance to succeed at hatching? Cash shop. Want to use the "digimon seals" that drop everywhere and make you stronger against certain breeds? Need to get the unlocker in  the cash shop.
It's worth looking at if you love Digimon, because god knows we don't get many oppertunities to show it, but 13 hours was enough for it to lose any favour in that regard for me. Go play a good game instead.

A nice little game, very similar to banished - but in space of course. The objective is to build and survive, which is not easily done,  It takes some strategic thinking and planning, with a decent learning curve, at least at first.
It is a fun game and I would recommend it to any city builder or banished fan. But it falls short for a few reasons;
Once you survive, build your base up and make it sustainable, the only thing left is to expand. While this can be fun for a while, theres no real threat to your existance, outside of bad planning or expanding too fast. It doesnt seem like you can run out of resources, nor have any outbreaks or virus's etc that might take a toll on your colony. The threats that do exist are manageable.
Buildings are almost all unlocked within the first 10mins of the game, theres no real research to be done and so there's nothing really to strive for. Sure you have to combine resources to build new things, and things you need - but thats a just a waiting game - which brings me to the last point;
Its a waiting game a lot of the time. AI can be a bit stupid and doesnt always do the right task in the right order. ie if your low on food, and theres plenty of things to make up a meal, then go and harvest the food and make them! .. they dont always. So because of this, and the amount of time it takes to make some of the ingredients to build an object, you can be sitting watching your colony work away for long periods of time, and not be building a whole lot. Or having stacks of buildings under construction and waiting for construction materials to be made (but the AI is too busy doing something else).
Overall though - its a fun game. I only paid $20 for it, and it kept me entertained for a decent amount of time. I'd replay it casually here and there, but once its mastered, its not a game I'd play religiously. And an experienced builder will master this one in a few hours.

